    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d574">

                <pb facs="0594" n="582" xml:id="pg582"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24546/35: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Nouméa</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacVitty</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nouméa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-21T23:00:00+11:00">November 21,
                            1941—11 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 22—5:43 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>28. Reference my telegram 22, October 22, 10 p.m. [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >a.m.</hi>] In a conversation with the High Commissioner today he said he
                    felt that any improvements in present air bases here should be subject of an
                    agreement between the Free French, Australia and American Governments and that
                    he was averse to any work being done until such an agreement was made. He
                    insisted that the matter should be handled through the Free French
                    representative at Washington, not here.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVitty</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
